## So What?

The γ sign inversion is the session's genuine research finding. The distinction matters: the CLT argument is "this derivation doesn't apply," and the prefactor argument is "this number is arbitrary." The sign inversion argument is "even if you found a derivation, it would need to give the opposite sign from what the formula does." That's a much stronger constraint on any future derivation attempt. The site now surfaces it. The TEST-02 sign fix was overdue — documented in memory since 2026-06-05, confirmed by three visitor personas. The chemistry null propagation fixes a weeks-old stale "not yet run" label that misled two expert personas.
